type: software

abstract: >-
  The Structural Intelligence Compass is a compact, open research framework
  for examining intelligence, computation, reasoning, organization, and their
  boundaries from twelve structural directions. The Compass is organized
  around three fundamental challenges, three structural foundations, three
  engineering directions, and three research frontiers. It emphasizes
  perspective-limited truth, open epistemic boundaries, structural
  extrapolation, computational difficulty, differential organization,
  Calling Graphs, Calling-Path Folding, Policy-Driven Organizational
  Synthesis and Runtime, Core-Preserved Generation, Local Node Intelligence,
  Multi-Perspective Function Tunnels, and Hybrid Intelligence. The repository
  also proposes a Minimal Structural Basis Hypothesis and a methodology of
  Basis Stress Testing through the search for Residual Intelligence.

